#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_eta1

#% text
# `weierstrass_eta1([g2, g3])` gives the quasi-period `eta1 = weierstrass_zeta(omega1, [g2, g3])`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `weierstrass_zeta(u + 2 omega_k, [g2, g3]) = weierstrass_zeta(u, [g2, g3]) + 2 eta_k` (DLMF 23.2.14), with the half-periods of `weierstrass_half_periods`.

#% item
# Legendre's relation `eta1 omega3 - eta3 omega1 = im pi/2` holds; `eta1 + eta2 + eta3 = 0`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_eta1([9.0, 3.0])
#% output
#= 0.8054423232280936

#% cell
n(weierstrass_eta1([23, 7]), 25)
#% output
#= 0.98398141010786928852371623984

#% cell
weierstrass_eta1([0.5 + im, 1.0])
#% output
#= 0.2854451328963893 - 0.5172503680562534im

#% cell
weierstrass_eta1([1, 0])
#% output
#= pi^(3/2)/gamma(1/4)^2

#% text
# The quasi-periodicity of zeta:

#% cell
w = weierstrass_half_period_w1([9.0, 3.0]); weierstrass_zeta(0.4 + 2*w, [9, 3]) - weierstrass_zeta(0.4, [9, 3]) - 2*weierstrass_eta1([9.0, 3.0])
#% output
#= -8.881784197001252e-16

